CAMUV extends CAM (Bühlmann et al. 2014) to handle latent confounders. Steps:
1. Preprocessing: transform variables to (approximately) Gaussian marginals (rank-based Gaussianization / NQ transform), like CAM.
2. Initial greedy DAG search over a large max parent-set size (q_max, e.g. 5) using additive-model score (weighted least squares with sub-binning / regression splines) + Gaussian likelihood score.
